  "description": "In this report, we analyze the compromise of Paperwork, starting with the discovery of an exposed source code archive on a web application. Reviewing the source code revealed an unauthenticated OS command injection vulnerability in a custom LPD-like service, yielding an initial foothold as the lp user. From there, local enumeration uncovered an internal JetDirect/PJL service vulnerable to path traversal, which was exploited to write an SSH key and pivot to the archivist user. Finally, a privileged daemon was abused to leak a root-opened file descriptor via SCM_RIGHTS, disclosing administrative credentials and granting full root access.",
